<p>Thailand&#x27;s parliament on Thursday elected Anutin Charnvirakul as prime minister, confirming that the Bhumjaithai Party leader will remain in office after a lower-house vote in Bangkok. The Hindu reported that Anutin won 293 votes, more than the majority required from the 498 lawmakers who attended the House of Representatives session. The vote gives Thailand a measure of political continuity as the country tries to move beyond years of political conflict and weak growth. But Anutin takes office under economic pressure tied to turmoil in the Middle East: SCMP reported that Thailand has been spending tens of millions of dollars a day to support fuel prices as queues form at petrol stations.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/RF9Q-5SThQrQvyE9x2yVn7aybKFG4dt1_jRfPazkCNl7AQT_d9sHlLtieBPIzgPq14jFlfy4o68TRCXl5tULKOaTy5TKfGazbN4jsRb33QXO_wfW2RZG3Vq1lnJ_Plrg_KOo8bt4LmvJo3D1677STBj_YTKyGfA4NrrZIF3mjg' alt='Image accompanying coverage of Thailand&#x27;s parliamentary vote for prime minister' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Expected confirmation: ABC described the parliamentary session as a vote in which the incumbent was expected to remain in office, making it more a formal confirmation than a suspenseful contest.</li><li>Post-election step: CBS19 said the re-election followed Bhumjaithai&#x27;s victory in the recent election, linking the parliamentary outcome to the party&#x27;s broader electoral win.</li><li>Smooth passage: SCMP reported that Anutin sailed through the lower-house vote, highlighting how smoothly the parliamentary process wrapped up.</li><li>International framing: Deutsche Welle described Anutin as a nationalist, emphasizing his political identity alongside the vote result.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Analysts cited by Deutsche Welle said Anutin&#x27;s selection could help steady Thailand after a prolonged period of political strain. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/thailand-elects-anutin-charnvirakul-as-new-prime-minister/a-76425154'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li><li>SCMP framed the vote as a win for Thailand&#x27;s conservative establishment after years of struggle with pro-democracy forces. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/southeast-asia/article/3347127/pm-anutin-takes-charge-thailand-mideast-chaos-pressures-economy'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>The Hindu focused on the parliamentary arithmetic, reporting that Anutin cleared the required majority in the House of Representatives. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/thailand-prime-minister-anutin-charnvirakul-to-remain-in-power-following-parliament-vote/article70760942.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/thai-parliament-convenes-vote-new-prime-minister-incumbent-131206429'>Thai Parliament convenes to vote for new PM with incumbent leader expected to stay</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/thailand-elects-anutin-charnvirakul-as-new-prime-minister/a-76425154'>Thailand elects Anutin Charnvirakul as new prime minister</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/thailand-prime-minister-anutin-charnvirakul-to-remain-in-power-following-parliament-vote/article70760942.ece'>Thailand Prime Minister Anutin Charnvirakul to remain in power following Parliament vote</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/southeast-asia/article/3347127/pm-anutin-takes-charge-thailand-mideast-chaos-pressures-economy'>PM Anutin takes charge in Thailand as Mideast chaos pressures economy</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbs19news.com/thailands-new-parliament-elects-anutin-as-pm/article_2669029c-9e0e-5f89-94df-f4531ebdca67.html'>The National Assembly of Thailand re-elects Anutin Charnvirakul as prime minister following his Bhumjaithai Party&#x27;s victory in the recent election.</a> - cbs19news.com</li></ul>